          to know what they are looking at, and it makes the ambiguity above
          something they can produce themselves rather than take on trust.
        */}
        <h3>Try it</h3>
        <p>
          Put a few errors in a line and watch the interior checks fall silent.
          A chain of length one and a chain of length five can leave the same
          two checks lit — that is the ambiguity the decoder has to resolve, and
          it is not a limitation of the measurement apparatus but of what a
          parity check is.
        </p>

        <SurfaceCode />

        <h2>Method</h2>
        <h3>Data</h3>
        <p>
          Syndromes were generated with circuit-level noise rather than a
          simplified independent-error model — the measurement apparatus is
          itself faulty, so the syndrome arrives as a noisy time series over
          repeated rounds and not as one clean snapshot. Training used tens of
          millions of shots; the model is only converged at that scale, and
          conclusions drawn from smaller runs were, repeatedly, artifacts.
        </p>

        <h3>Model</h3>
        <p>
          A recurrent stage consumes the rounds in order and a convolutional
          stage exploits the fact that the lattice is spatially local and the
          same everywhere. The network predicts one bit — whether a logical
          flip has occurred — because that is the only question with a
          well-defined answer.
        </p>

        <figure>
          <img
            src={FIGURES[1].src}
            alt={FIGURES[1].alt}
            width={FIGURES[1].width}
            height={FIGURES[1].height}
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <figcaption>{FIGURES[1].caption}</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h3>Evaluation</h3>
        <p>
          Against matching on an identical held-out set of shots, with paired
          statistics rather than two independently reported numbers — the
          comparison of interest is per-shot agreement and disagreement, which
          a pair of aggregate error rates throws away.
        </p>
        <p>
          Run-to-run variation turned out to be large enough to swamp the
          effect being measured, so every reported number is a mean over
          independent training runs with a band, and single-run results are not
          treated as evidence.
        </p>

