        <p>
          The failure analysis was the part that changed how I thought about
          the problem. Errors are not uniformly distributed across the lattice,
          and looking at the actual circuit at the moment a shot fails is far
          more informative than another point on an error-rate curve.
        </p>

        <h2>Current status</h2>
        <p>
          Ongoing. The current thread is quantization: a decoder that has to
          run inside the control loop of a real machine has to fit on an FPGA
          and finish inside the error-correction cycle, so the interesting
          question is no longer just accuracy but how much precision can be
          removed from the weights before accuracy goes with it.
        </p>

